  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb — follows standard -AR endings with no exceptions (the two adjacent vowels *e-a* in the stem never trigger a spelling change)",
    "Past participle: *paseado* (regular)",
    "Means \"to walk\" or \"to take a stroll\" (for pleasure, not as a means of transport) — *pasear por el parque* (to stroll through the park)",
    "Also used transitively meaning \"to walk\" (someone/something) — *pasear al perro* (to walk the dog)",
    "Reflexive form *pasearse* is common too, with the same basic meaning: *me paseé por la playa* (I strolled along the beach)",
    "Related: *paseo* (walk, stroll, also \"avenue/promenade\" as in *Paseo de la Reforma*), *paseante* (stroller, walker)"
  ],
